(Discrepancy 2 repro — `fork` is in the Statement Starters table (4642) and
 so is claimed to be reserved (4696), but a variable may be declared with
 that name. Reading it does not read the variable: the fork EXPRESSION wins,
 so the program silently forks and the value 42 is unreachable. The child
 exits immediately here; without that Exit the rest of the program would run
 twice.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D2.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   a child process appeared that the program never asked for
   reading the variable named fork forked instead of reading 42
)
a number called fork is 42.
Set observed to fork.
If observed is 0 then,
    Print "a child process appeared that the program never asked for",
    Exit 0.
Set reaped to reap any child process.
If observed is 42 then,
    Print "the variable was read".
If observed is not 42 then,
    Print "reading the variable named fork forked instead of reading 42".
